<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sun Tzu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 500 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a> · Also known as Sunzi, Sun Wu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sun Tzu (Sunzi, Sun Wu) is the traditional author of The Art of War, the most famous Chinese work on military strategy. According to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/records-of-the-grand-historian">Shiji</a> he was a general from Qi who served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-helu-of-wu">King Helü of Wu</a> around 500 BCE, though many historians doubt this and date the text to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warring-states-period">Warring States period</a>. The book stresses deception, intelligence and winning without fighting.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sun-tzu.jpg" alt="Sun Tzu" width="276" height="300" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%90%B4%E5%8F%B8%E9%A9%AC%E5%AD%99%E6%AD%A6.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
